A hybrid document whose header is badly spaced and whose body is ragged
SQL. SQL-mode data sources get no edits from the formatter at all, header
included (feature.formatting A9): the formatter would otherwise inject
semicolons into the SQL. Diagnostics stay on the header only.
-- input.ds --
:DSN:=DATABASE;
:PARAMETERS   sKind := "X" ,nTop := 10;
select   kind_code,kind_label
   from kind_lookup
      where kind_code = @sKind
-- format --
:DSN:=DATABASE;
:PARAMETERS   sKind := "X" ,nTop := 10;
select   kind_code,kind_label
   from kind_lookup
      where kind_code = @sKind
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
